'Subject: thanks ! !\r\njust a note to tell each of you that i appreciate your efforts today in our\r\nlengthy meeting . i think you all were very professional , and you all asked\r\nthe right questions of each other . i was very proud of the level of\r\nperformance i saw today , and think this group has strengthened over the last\r\nsix months , which was one of our goals . the challenges today were healthy\r\nand with merit . i realize it is a difficult process , but i appreciate your\r\npatience to work through the process . i know each of you realize the\r\nimportance of our building a strong team , as we are only as strong as our\r\npeople . we are required to identify strengths and weaknesses to help the\r\nemployee become stronger . enron is the best , and we are obligated to build\r\nthe very best teams to ensure we deliver the very best services . if we do\r\nnot , we all fail .\r\ngood job , today . once again , thank you .',ham
'Subject: cilco\r\nper our conversation , the months relating to the cilco deal with ena - texas\r\nare may 1999 - sept 1999 .\r\nhowever , when howard and i talked about correcting the allocation in pops ,\r\nhoward is telling me that the cilco sale is tied to the transport ( 206 )\r\ncontract in pops . if we remove the sale b / t ena - tx and cilco and put the\r\nsale b / t ena - tx and the storage book , we no longer have a sale to tie to the\r\ntransport . let me know what you think as we did not discuss this .\r\nthanks !',ham
